<h2>Contact the grievance officer</h2>
<p><strong>Name:</strong> {'{{GRIEVANCE_OFFICER_NAME}}'}<br /><strong>Email:</strong> {'{{GRIEVANCE_EMAIL}}'}<br /><strong>Postal address:</strong> {'{{REG_ADDRESS}}'}</p>
<p>Use <a href="/report">Report a user</a> for a call complaint. Include your contact details, the profile name, call ID, and a clear account of what happened. Do not send passwords, OTPs, or Aadhaar details.</p>
<h2>Our response</h2>
<p>We aim to acknowledge a complaint within 24 hours and resolve it within 15 days, following the grievance process under the IT Rules 2021. Some categories may have shorter legal deadlines. We will explain any further information needed and tell you the outcome.</p>
<h2>If you need to escalate</h2>
<ol><li>Reply to the acknowledgement with your complaint reference and any missing facts.</li><li>Ask the grievance officer to review the outcome if you disagree or the response is overdue.</li><li>If still unresolved, you may use any appeal or complaint route available under applicable law, including the relevant Grievance Appellate Committee where it applies.</li></ol>
<p>This inbox is not an emergency service. If there is immediate danger, call <a href="tel:112">Emergency 112</a>.</p>
</HelloFraandsPage>
